# A2/A2.1/A2_02_restaurant_and_ordering.letz
# Source: PDF slide decks "L2 (Part 1)/(Part 2) a21convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A2.1, Lektioun 2).
# Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered pages, then every
# lemma verified against LOD (gender -> article; glosses cross-checked).
# Split from the deck's second half (A2.03) to keep each lesson near 40-60 Elements:
# this file is the restaurant scene and its vocabulary, A2.03 is the polite/conditional
# register (hätt/géif) built on top of it.
# Grammar focus: restaurant prepositions and modal verbs with a bare infinitive;
# `well` sends the finite verb to the end of its clause.

@lesson A2.02 "Restaurant & Ordering"

# --- Menu & courses ---
@word den Aperitif = the aperitif
@word d'Menüskaart = the menu card
@word d'Wäikaart = the wine list
@word d'Entrée = the starter
@word den Haaptplat = the main course
@word den Dagesmenü = the daily menu
@word den Dessert = the dessert
@word d'Rechnung = the bill

# --- Food & drink ---
@word d'Zopp = the soup
@word d'Zalot = the salad
@word de Bifdeck = the steak
@word de Räis = the rice
@word d'Fritten = the chips
@word de Poulet = the chicken
@word de Béier = the beer
@word d'Gedrénks = the beverage

# --- Cutlery ---
@word d'Forschett = the fork
@word d'Messer = the knife
@word de Läffel = the spoon
@word d'Zerwéit = the napkin

# --- Describing the food ---
@word bluddeg = rare
@word gutt duerch = well done
@word zéi = tough
@word versalzt = too salty

# --- Verbs & expressions ---
@word wielen = to choose
@word schmaachen = to taste
@word deelen = to share
@word w.e.g. = please

@sentence
@lu Hutt Dir reservéiert?
@en Have you reserved?
@distractor-en chosen
@distractor-en bill
@distractor-lu gewielt
@distractor-lu Rechnung

@sentence
@lu Wëllt Dir en Aperitif?
@en Do you want an aperitif?
