# --- @fill: `well` clauses and modal verbs ----------------------------------
# Each modal takes its bare infinitive. Distractors are wrong persons of that
# same modal, so the learner must choose the form that agrees with the subject.

@fill
@lu Ech drénke Waasser, well ech muer fuere [muss].
@en I drink water because I [have] to drive tomorrow.
@distractor-lu musst
@distractor-lu mussen
@distractor-lu musse
@distractor-en has
@distractor-en had
@distractor-en having

@fill
@lu Dir [kënnt] d'Rechnung elo bezuelen.
@en You [can] pay the bill now.
@distractor-lu kann
@distractor-lu kanns
@distractor-lu kënnen
@distractor-en could
@distractor-en cannot
@distractor-en will

@fill
@lu Du [wëlls] kee Béier drénken.
@en You [want] no beer to drink.
@distractor-lu wëll
@distractor-lu wëllt
@distractor-lu wëllen
@distractor-en wants
@distractor-en wanted
@distractor-en wanting

@fill
@lu Mir [sollen] haut de Serveur ruffen.
@en We [should] call the waiter today.
@distractor-lu soll
@distractor-lu solls
@distractor-lu sollt
@distractor-en must
@distractor-en may
@distractor-en can

@fill
@lu Ech [däerf] hei net fëmmen.
@en I [may] not smoke here.
@distractor-lu däerfs
@distractor-lu däerft
@distractor-lu däerfen
@distractor-en must
@distractor-en can
@distractor-en should

